        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Philippines, US and allies start military exercises testing 'real‑world' readiness Issued on: 20/04/2026 - 15:44 Philippine and US forces will carry out maritime strike drills on a remote Philippine island near Taiwan during annual exercises that started on Monday, which Manila's military chief said would ​test their readiness under \"real-world ‌conditions\". The April 20 to May 8 exercises known as \"Balikatan\", or \"shoulder-to-shoulder\", will be ⁠the largest yet in terms of participating countries, with Australia included again and Canada, France, New Zealand and Japan joining as active participants for the first ‌time. Israel army warns Lebanese against returning to south 20/04/2026 Iran-US ceasefire talks: Nuclear program remains sticking point 20/04/2026 20/04/2026 Israel army says established 'Yellow Line' in Lebanon, as in Gaza 20/04/2026 US seizes Iranian-flagged cargo ship 20/04/2026 Middle East 'US military leverage a risky tactic': Bombs, military escalation will not bring Iran 'to the table' 20/04/2026 Middle East UK PM Starmer under pressure over Mandelson's appointment as ambassador 20/04/2026 Rumen Radev, pro-Russia ex-pilot who wants to give Bulgaria wings 20/04/2026 Peace talks clouded by uncertainty after US seizes Iranian ship 20/04/2026"
